  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/C/#radio-button-group\r\n\r\nThe specification defines whether element *b* is in a radio button group or not if the group already contains element *a*.  However the specification says nothing about how to create a new radio button group.  The specification doesn't have answers for the following questions:\r\n - Should `<input type=checkbox>` be in a radio button group?\r\n - Should a radio button without `name` attribute be in a radio button group?\r\n - Should a radio button with a non-empty `name` attribute make a new radio button group if no suitable radio button group exist?\r\n\r\nBrowser implementations:\r\n - Major browsers agree that radio buttons with non-empty name attribute automatically create or join to a radio button group.\r\n - EdgeHTML and Firefox assume a radio button without `name` attribute is in a single-member radio button group, and Safari and Chrome assume it is not in any radio button groups.  It's observable by `input.validity.valueMissing` for `<input type=radio required>`.\r\n",
